  "intro": "This is your comprehensive A1 review covering everything from the alphabet and pronouns through cases, verb conjugation, adjective agreement, and prepositions. If you can handle these exercises, you have a solid A1 foundation and are ready for A2. Take your time — this review tests all major topics from the entire A1 level.",
  "rules": [
    "Nouns have three genders: masculine (consonant ending), feminine (-а/-я), neuter (-о/-е). Gender determines pronoun, adjective, and verb agreement.",
    "Russian has six cases. At A1, focus on nominative (subject), accusative (direct object), and prepositional (location with в/на).",
    "Present tense verbs conjugate in two patterns: 1st conjugation (-ю, -ешь, -ет, -ем, -ете, -ют) and 2nd conjugation (-ю, -ишь, -ит, -им, -ите, -ят).",
    "Adjectives and possessives agree with nouns in gender, number, and case: мой новый дом (m), моя новая книга (f), моё новое окно (n).",
    "Negation: не before verbs (Я не работаю), нет + genitive for 'don't have' (У меня нет книги). Questions use кто, что, где, когда, почему, как."
  ],
  "examples": [
    "Я читаю новую книгу в школе. (I read a new book at school.) — verb, adjective agreement, accusative, prepositional",
    "У моего брата нет машины. (My brother doesn't have a car.) — possession, genitive after нет",
    "Эти большие дома очень красивые. (These big houses are very beautiful.) — demonstrative, adjective, plural",
    "Почему ты не говоришь по-русски? (Why don't you speak Russian?) — question word, negation, verb"
